WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.230
Pedestrian Safety

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.230
If you cross in haste,
you may end up getting hit
by a passing car

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.230
Joutou
Elementary
Crossing
Safety
Haiku

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.230
Episode 6
Homeland

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.240
<i>Wakana-chan, how have you been?</i>

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.250
<i>By the time this letter reaches you,</i>

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.290
Aoba

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.290
Guesthouse

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.640
<i>I'll probably be in Aomori.</i>

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.290
Sawamura, come help with the luggage!

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.210
<i>I'm here for a training camp.</i>

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.630
<i>If you ask how things turned out
like this in the first place...</i>

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.920
Umezono Private Academy

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.920
One and a Half Months Earlier

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.920
Our "Roku-dan" seems to be
shaping up pretty well, doesn't it?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.990
U-Um... Sawamura-kun?

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.680
Are you listening?

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.510
Huh?

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:41.120
Um... Do you think we could
start practicing "Shinbushi"?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.480
I suppose that'd be fine.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.210
All right!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.440
No...

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:52.060
Th-Things can't continue like this...

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.630
Maimai...

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.270
...will beat me!

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.000
Yui-chan!

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.820
Maimai is a girl from Aomori
I met through an online game.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.040
Apparently, she's entering the Tsugaru
Shamisen Koshien group division, too.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:05.830
Maimai the Snail

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.980
And when I listened to them play...

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
Yutti MegMeg

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
Tomoyan Shirocchi

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
Runpa

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
Let's do our best together!!

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.540
"Group practice"

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.670
Like

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.670
Comment

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.590
We're like a party of weaklings that's
only just made it out of the first town!

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.880
I don't <i>ever</i> want to be beaten!
Not in games and not in shamisen!

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.500
It's time for some serious training!

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.080
Aomori? Maimai?

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.640
<i>Her obsessive persistence led to everyone
memorizing "Shinbushi" within a month.</i>

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.140
<i>And then...</i>

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.400
I see.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.650
These nails and fingertips...

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.830
It seems you've done an
incredible amount of practicing.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.450
Traditional Japanese Instrument Shop Owner
Oodawara Hiroshi

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.450
And on top of that...

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.690
What is this firm texture I see that
only comes from many years of playing?

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.330
Release the hands of my male students!

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.080
I see.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.230
Your passion speaks right to my heart.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.750
This must be fate, brought about by
the repair of Kamiki Seiryuu's shamisen.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.920
Let's go on a training camp
when summer vacation starts.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.840
In Aomori!

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.010
What?

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.600
It <i>has</i> to be in Tsugaru, right?!

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.680
Well, this is sudden.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:03.520
It'll be expensive.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.970
It's a little, uh...

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:28.500
Those Snow White Notes

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.610
Aoba Guesthouse

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.510
Having all this space to use as we please...

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.490
Thank you so much!

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.080
Think nothing of it.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.230
Work hard, now.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.420
<i>No matter how fired up we are,
we're still beginners.</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.300
<i>There's only so much we can do.</i>

00:03:59.300 --> 00:03:59.840
<i>But...</i>

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.970
<i>It's been a long time since I got fired up
about something and practiced this hard.</i>

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.200
<i>I </i>will<i> defeat Maimai!</i>

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.680
<i>I'm gonna use this training
camp to rack up EXP!</i>

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.950
<i>Wow, this is Kamiki
Seiryuu's futozao all right.</i>

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.890
<i>It's a </i>little<i> quirky,
but it has a robust resonance.</i>

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.160
<i>I can't get enough of it!</i>

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.300
<i>Nagamori-kun's experience with the hosozao
has given him some impressive skills.</i>

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.430
<i>And...</i>

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.340
<i>Sawamura-kun really is extraordinary.</i>

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:34.260
<i>It's such a waste that he isn't
entering the individual division.</i>

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.510
<i>The one I can't help worrying about is...</i>

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:43.900
<i>I did it again.</i>

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.140
<i>I messed up the timing again.</i>

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.990
<i>What? What do I do now?</i>

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:55.140
<i>I don't know what I'm supposed
to be playing anymore!</i>

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.280
All right! Let's stop there for today.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.510
Thank you very much.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.070
Good work today.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.640
Shuri, don't be so down.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.470
Is this the dreaded "slump"?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.250
Ah, all this gloom is annoying! Go take
a bath and wash off your blues, will ya?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.040
'Kay.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.710
<i>Sawamura-kun hasn't said anything...</i>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.300
<i>This whole time...</i>

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.280
<i>...that sound has stayed in my head.</i>

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.140
<i>It was a sensation I'd never felt before...</i>

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.680
If it's the shamisen that gives you life,

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.810
then one day, whether you will it or not,
that world is going to drag you in.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.600
Um... Sawamura-kun?

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:45.950
Huh? Yeah?

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:48.940
About my playing...

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:52.570
I wasn't listening closely, but keep
playing like that and you'll be fine.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.570
What?

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.210
Hey!

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.650
Quit condescending to us.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.520
There's no way it's fine for
her to be so off all the time!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.540
Then, she should fix that.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.550
You little...

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.680
She's asking <i>you</i> because
she doesn't know <i>how</i> to fix it!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.280
I don't know how to, either!

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:11.560
H-Hold on!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.560
It's true. Sawamura probably
<i>wouldn't</i> know how to.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.000
Kai-chan, please stop!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.640
It's my fault for playing
so badly. So please...

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.990
And if we displease Mr. Genius here, he might
not play with us in the competition, right?

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.410
You don't even wanna do this,
yet you've got people fawning all over you.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.490
Even though you've got a ring to fight in...

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.370
Life isn't something
you can take for granted.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:44.250
Just looking at guys like you who waste
their talents makes my blood boil!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.230
Now that I think about it,
you don't know, do you, Sawamura?

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:03.560
Kaito played soccer for a super long time,
and he was expected to go far.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.570
But not long after starting high school...

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:08.470
Kaito!

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.790
Are you okay?!

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:12.860
He couldn't carry on like before.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:17.480
On top of that, his father's
a lawyer for prominent politicians,

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.090
and he expects Kaito to
follow in his footsteps.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.300
So he gave up on his dreams of going pro.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.060
That's why he gets so irritated
watching you, I'm sure.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.470
Men

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.520
Dear, about Kaito's injury...

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.440
It's a good thing.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.770
It means he can devote himself to his studies.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.110
Even if he had gone into sports,
there isn't much future in it.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:54.040
<i>I'm someone who's been perfectly set
on the rails my parents laid down.</i>

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.290
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.120
So you heard, huh?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:16.050
You've got no goals and no motivation.
The one thing you do have is talent.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.510
From my perspective,
it's pretty infuriating.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.220
You're self-centered and moody...

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.770
Your accent's indecipherable sometimes...

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.420
And you've got angry eyes.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.400
But...

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:30.900
It's not your fault I can't
play soccer anymore.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.020
That's just how you are. Sorry for snapping.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:36.740
It's fine.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:40.910
Hey... You're really not gonna
enter the individual division?

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.220
Lately, when I look at you...

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.900
No, never mind. It's none of my business, is it?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.270
Ah, the wonders of youth!

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.440
Blabbermouth.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.950
That's freezing!

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.820
Really! What do you think you're doing?!

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.920
Huh? Wh-What's going on?

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.950
They're just goofing around
naked. It's a guy thing.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.350
It is?

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.830
Take this!

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.700
Now you've done it!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:17.700
That must mean they've made up, then.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.490
Dear...

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:21.660
Hm?

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.690
It looks like Umeko-san's
making a move after all.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:27.870
And like usual, she's
chosen the flashy route.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.320
It seems she wants to make Setsu-kun known...

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:36.370
as the successor to the genius
shamisen player, Sawamura Matsugorou.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.760
I'm really looking forward to it.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:46.060
<i>According to Kousuke, Sawamura Setsu's
only competing in the group division.</i>

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>I'll win!</i>

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.560
<i>I'll never let him beat me!</i>

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:57.240
<i>Dad looked up to old Matsugorou.</i>

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.450
Well, then...

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.870
Might be fun to bring the
winner's trophy home with me.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.090
Behold, children!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.120
The Tsugaru Strait!

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.700
On the other side of it,
you'll see that "Hokkaido is huge-o"!

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:22.510
He certainly is lively
first thing in the morning.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.480
But you already know that,
right, Sawamura-kun?

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.740
I wonder if you kids know this...

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.910
In the Edo period, when
there was still a class system,

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:30.430
the predecessors of the
Tsugaru shamisen style

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:34.240
were affiliated with the Toudouza,
a guild for blind men.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.430
In the name of the movie <i>Zatoichi</i>, the "zato"
part refers to one of the ranks in this guild.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.210
Huh. Really?

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:41.080
Wow...

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.310
And the majority of the men were very poor.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.250
They were oppressed and persecuted.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.680
Even after the Meiji Restoration,
their daily lives didn't change.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:56.040
They were met with scorn and disdain,
and made to wander the provinces.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.410
They played their shamisens
in front of house after house,

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.970
living day to day on the food
or money they received.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.980
They could not see, but if you put zeni
coins in the cloths around their necks,

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.370
they could hear the clinking of the coins,

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.850
and if it was food you put there,
they could feel the weight of it.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:17.360
Their lives depended on
that sound and that weight.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:19.970
They endured starvation
and frigid temperatures.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.270
And when the cold eased, they would set
out once more on their journey for their lives.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.670
Those men could not see the
beauty of the scenery around them.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:32.700
I wonder what the hearts of
the people looked like to them.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:37.260
<i>I'm sure that Gramps, for better or worse,</i>

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:40.330
<i>could sense every subtlety in
the depths of people's hearts.</i>

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:46.290
Then, time passed, and change came.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:51.680
People drawn to the sound of the
futozao wanted to carry on the music.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:57.190
And they were people like us.
People who were not blind.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.010
There were no barriers
or limitations for them.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.950
I think the power of the futozao
and the rhythms it produces

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.200
are like the soul of the Japanese people.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.750
What we call "the blues."

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.880
Traditions? Rules?

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:13.960
I don't think anything so formal or
stuck-up existed in the first place.

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:17.670
After all, even the founder of the
Tsugaru shamisen style, Nitaboh,

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.380
and his apprentices, and <i>their</i> apprentices,

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:24.660
plus musicians of today, are constantly
pushing boundaries, trying out new things.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.230
The style changes with the times.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:31.410
That's precisely why it gets passed
down and has carried on like it has.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.720
Tsugaru shamisen has
surpassed Tsugaru itself!

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.360
That's why even people who know
nothing about Tsugaru can still play it.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:43.550
But there are a couple of things
I want you never to forget...

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:49.330
How remarkable our predecessors
who established this sound were,

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.370
and how much respect they deserve.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.740
Please don't ever forget those things.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.120
<i>My sound was passed down from
Gramps' teacher to Gramps,</i>

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:00.700
<i>and then, to Wakana-chan and me.</i>

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.590
Sawamura-kun?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.850
<i>So that's it, huh?</i>

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.950
<i>Maybe that's what it means...</i>

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.520
<i>... to find my sound.</i>

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.490
Now, then!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.550
I'll be playing some lovely,
robust sounds again today!

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:28.570
What?

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:29.360
Huh?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.870
Kaito gets Kamiki Seiryuu's one.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.580
What  What do you mean?

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.460
If you're being nice to me
because of yesterday...

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:36.460
It's not that.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.480
For Rai-senpai, a shamisen
with no quirks will allow

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.630
his delicate hosozao
techniques shine through.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.440
Kaito's strong, and his
arms and wrists are steady,

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.380
so I think he'll make this shamisen sing.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.640
Sing?

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.580
Strike it with everything you've got.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:57.150
<i>Can someone like me... be like
Kamiki Seiryuu... and Sawamura...</i>

00:13:57.470 --> 00:14:00.850
<i>and make the air tremble?</i>

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:05.400
<i>I'll do it!</i>

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.970
Think you'll be able to
get out of your slump?

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:11.040
I-I don't know. I'm not confident at all.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:15.120
Maeda-san isn't quite catching the cue
''the ai-no-te'' when we shout "hai."

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:18.680
Why don't we have you practice
on your own until you get the timing?

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.360
I'm sorry.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.660
Sawamura-kun.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.210
You must be pleased. You have a visitor.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.710
Hey, Setsu.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.640
This watermelon's from my place.
Share it with everyone.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.180
It said in your letter you'd be here,

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.060
so I brought Wakana-chan 'cause
I thought you might be missing him.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:38.220
Not really.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:38.940
What?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.440
How can you say that to your
one and only older brother?!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.060
Now, now...

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:43.710
Older brother?

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:47.000
Setsu! I went to the trouble
of coming all the way out here!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.510
The one in the sunglasses is?
Not the cauliflower head?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.290
Huh? That's not his dad?

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.070
They don't look anything alike, do they?

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:52.580
For real?

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:55.180
Setsu, you're entering
the individual competition?

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:57.320
Umeko entered me without asking, that's all.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.670
I'll come cheer for you!
You'd better do your best!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.340
Are you even listening?

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.890
You're not gonna do it?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:06.410
To be honest, I'm not sure.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:08.800
Right now, I'm fifty-fifty
about wanting to play in it.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.230
<i>Wanting to "play," huh? Not "win."</i>

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.220
<i>Though, even that's a huge change.</i>

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.080
<i>I just wish he'd be a little greedier.</i>

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.610
I wonder what Gramps would
say if he were still alive.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.360
Well...

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.640
It's true he wasn't interested
in competitions at all,

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.660
and he never had any apprentices.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:36.360
I thought the lack of apprentices was weird,
too, so I asked him about it. And he said...

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:40.300
Anyone who <i>really</i> listens when I play,

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.960
will be able to learn my sound, anyway.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.730
Everyone is like an apprentice to me.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:51.840
That's a clever thing to say,
but that's not going to help anyone learn.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:52.800
Right?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:57.820
But as long as there are people who
<i>really</i> listened and still remember,

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.800
Gramps' sound will never disappear.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:02.010
That's what it means, right?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.240
Oh!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.430
In that case,

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:10.770
Setsu should play in the tournament
so that more people can really listen to it!

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:13.190
Nice one, Kouta!

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:15.110
That's exactly what I wanted to say!

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.180
Setsu! It's a done deal!

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:20.160
<i>It's so obvious they're trying
to light a fire under me.</i>

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.210
<i>Hey, Gramps.</i>

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:29.800
<i>If you heard my sound now...</i>

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.350
<i>What would you say?</i>

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:36.090
Later, Setsu.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:37.450
Yeah.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.930
What I told you earlier
about what Gramps said...

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.540
He added something else.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:43.600
Something else?

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:49.140
The people who listened to him play and
remembered his sound were like apprentices...

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:50.950
But...

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.520
it's the reactions of the people listening
that are the most important lessons.

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.890
Once you know that,

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:03.620
even if I did take on apprentices,
there'd be nothing I could teach them.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.910
<i>That's true.</i>

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.940
<i>If no one listens, I won't
be able to find my sound.</i>

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:25.800
<i>I don't want this training camp...</i>

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:28.830
<i>to end without me having learned anything.</i>

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>For now, all I can do is work hard!</i>

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:41.610
Huh?

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.550
Cape

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.550
Tappimi
(Dragonsflight)

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.050
<i>This sound!</i>

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:27.720
<i>It's Sawamura-kun's sound.</i>

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:41.480
<i>The sound... It's overflowing!</i>

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:43.080
Wa!

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.640
"Wa"?

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:55.270
I-I'm so sorry...

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:56.630
I interrupted you.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:02.010
Um... Was that your "Shinkyuubushi"
for the individual competition just now?

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.260
Yeah.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.780
I... um... When I heard it...

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:11.100
For some reason... this feeling rose up
in my chest and I felt I had to shout.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.790
You don't have to fight that feeling, you know.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.820
That's what ai-no-te are.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:21.370
Then was the timing of my ai-no-te okay?

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.800
The timing was fine.
It was a weird noise, though.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.340
B-But still! I did it!

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:30.810
You see, just now, I wasn't
chasing the sound, I was riding it!

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.250
Sawamura-kun, your sound was
leaping so freely, it felt amazing!

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:38.860
D-Did I say something strange?

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:43.080
No, you didn't.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.380
Thanks.

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:47.480
What? Wh-Why are you thanking me?

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:50.930
You've given me the last little
push I needed, Maeda-san.

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:51.740
What?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.540
I will...

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.040
...compete in the individual division.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.370
Okay!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.850
Aoba Guesthouse

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.560
''A Few Days Later''

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.350
We did it.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.860
That was wonderful, everyone!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.810
We did it, Shuri! We played it with no mistakes!

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.850
I'm so glad...

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:13.740
But still, what <i>was</i> that? My ears are burning.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:16.980
What are you talking about?
It's the shamisen singing.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:18.830
What? It's singing?

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.220
Sawamura! Is mine singing?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:22.790
Yes.

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:24.090
All right!

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.970
All right, everyone.
You've worked very hard.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:30.590
As you're all returning to Tokyo tomorrow,
allow me to help you make some memories!

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:33.500
I give you permission to
attend the festival tonight!

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.860
Festival?

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:49.420
Just what you'd expect from Nebuta,
one of the three great festivals of Tohoku!

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.710
It's all so snappable!

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:53.040
This is insane! The grilled squid is so good!

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.200
The grilled corn is amazing, too!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.390
Huh? You're eating <i>two</i> candied apples?

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.860
This is how I do Nebuta.

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:01.200
They're that good, huh? Lemme have a bite!

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:03.040
It seems Sawamura-kun has decided to
participate in the individual division,

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:03.040
Cut it out. You'll pass on your germs to me.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:05.810
Germs? What are you talking about?
Just let me have a bite!

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:07.400
so if the hard work Maeda-san and the others
have put in as beginners yields results...

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:06.550
No.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:09.450
C'mon, just one bite. What harm will it do?

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:11.390
Well, that all depends on what it depends on.
You never know, you know?

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:12.720
All men turn back into kids at festivals.

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.420
They're having fun goofing off.

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.620
So true.

00:22:14.420 --> 00:22:15.630
No, we're not!

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:24.400
Sponsored by

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:24.400
Umemaru

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:24.400
National High School Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:24.400
Matsugorou Cup Opening Press Conference

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:24.400
Approved by: PLUM Corporation, Beauty UME, International U, et al.

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:22.200
Okay, well... Sawamura Matsugorou.

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:24.650
If I had to describe him as
a person, I'd say he was...

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:27.660
a musician native to this
region who had no ambitions.

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:33.080
But the color and quality of his sound shook
the hearts of musicians and listeners alike.

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:35.390
That was the great genius
that poured out of him.

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:41.270
As his daughter, as a way
to enjoy Tsugaru shamisen,

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:39.040
Your son has made the decision

00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:39.040
to enter the individual competition

00:22:41.270 --> 00:22:45.550
and in the hopes that it will remain
a familiar sound, not a rarely-heard one,

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:49.490
I will endeavor to carve out
another path going forward.

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:54.910
I hope for your continued support. of the Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien.
